# An unknown string escape -- here `\ ` (backslash-space) -- is invalid: only
# \n \t \r \\ \" are valid string escapes (`\r` was added by the friction plan;
# tychoc0 stops at \n \t \\ \" and this fixture is chosen to be rejected by
# both). tychoc rejected this at lex time, but
# tychoc0 silently ACCEPTED it (fail-open: it skipped the escaped byte without
# validating, then emitted a C string literal gcc would mangle). The reject-fuzzer
# surfaced it as an accept/reject divergence (divergence_6). Both lexers now reject.
fn main():
    println("oops\ here")
